  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_t4m1769 turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Can we talk?" Saltanat sits down near you. "Just... talk. Like people used to."
    NPC: "Come see what I found. You won't believe it."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: It's quiet at the hollow. Saltanat doesn't say much. Sometimes that's the whole point.
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Any regrets? The real kind, not the small stuff."
    YOU: "I didn't say what I needed to say. To someone. Now I can't."
    NPC: Quiet. "Yeah. I think everyone's carrying one of those."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on your regrets."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on your regrets."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on your regrets. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Can I ask you something else?"
    NPC: "I'll keep it to myself. What's on your mind?"
    YOU: "Anything on your mind lately?"
    NPC: "You asked me that before. It's a different question now." "Have you felt it? Like the air before a storm, but — bigger. Something's on its way."
    YOU: "Yes."
    NPC: They nod. "Okay."
    YOU: "I’m listening."
    NPC: "That's... pretty much all of it, honestly."
    NPC: "Rest when you can. We'll talk again soon."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You say nothing. Neither do they, for a while — and it's fine.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "It's been a while. Glad we circled back to what's been happening."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

