  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request stan_kowalski turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "About that question — What's something from your old life that's actually useful here?"
    YOU: "Patience. Sounds dumb. But waiting — really waiting, without fidgeting — that's a superpower now."
    NPC: "Not dumb at all. The people who can't wait are the ones who make mistakes. You're an asset."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: They pull back half a step — not leaving, just... further.
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Being an exterminator taught me to read people fast — who's lying, who's scared, who needs a job. Turns out that's a survival skill. Who knew."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on your useful old-life skills."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on your useful old-life skills."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Okay, real question: what's the funniest thing you've seen since we got here? I desperately need it."
    YOU: (tell them something funny)
    NPC: They laugh — really laugh, the first real one you've heard in days. "Okay. Okay, that's good. I needed that."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Me? I laughed yesterday and it scared me — the sound of it. Like my body remembered something my head hadn't approved. Laughter's a mutiny. A good one."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on your useful old-life skills. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Well. My social battery is officially dead."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You don't answer. The quiet turns pointed.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Good — your useful old-life skills, settled. Feels better said out loud."
    NPC: They nod, already turning away.

